The Receiving Party shall:
(a) use the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information only for the Purpose;
(b) disclose it only to its employees, directors, professional advisers and subcontractors who need to know it for the Purpose and are bound by written confidentiality obligations no less protective than this Agreement;
(c) protect it with at least reasonable care and no less care than it applies to its own confidential information; and
(d) promptly notify the Disclosing Party of any unauthorised use or disclosure of which it becomes aware.

Clause 3 does not apply to information that:
(a) is or becomes public other than through breach of this Agreement;
(b) was lawfully known to the Receiving Party before disclosure;
(c) is lawfully obtained from a third party without restriction; or
(d) is independently developed by the Receiving Party without use of the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information.

WHEREAS, AtliQ provides data engineering, analytics and AI/ML services to its clients, and requires certain data preparation and annotation services in connection with a client project;
WHEREAS, AtliQ desires to engage Vendor to provide such services, and Vendor desires to provide such services, subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement;
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements set forth herein, the Parties agree as follows:

The Recipient shall:
(a) use the Confidential Information solely for the purpose of evaluating and, if applicable, performing the Proposed Transaction;
(b) keep the Confidential Information strictly confidential and not disclose it to any person other than its Representatives who need to know it and are bound by obligations at least as protective as this Agreement;
(c) apply security measures no less stringent than those required under the Company's information-security policy as notified to the Recipient from time to time; and
(d) be responsible for any breach of this Agreement by its Representatives.

Distributor Portal v2
(a) Credit-limit visibility and online payment reconciliation for distributors;
(b) Scheme and promotion eligibility calculator;
(c) Mobile-responsive redesign and Malayalam / Tamil language support;
(d) Integration with the Client's ERP for real-time stock availability.

Sales Performance Dashboard
(a) Power BI dashboard covering primary and secondary sales by region, distributor, SKU and salesperson;
(b) Target-vs-actual tracking and scheme ROI analysis;
(c) Weekly automated email summaries to regional sales managers.

Supplier shall design, implement and hand over a new data ingestion and processing layer for the Platform, comprising in particular:
(a) streaming ingestion of machine sensor data (OPC UA / MQTT) from Client's customers' plants into Client's EU cloud environment;
(b) a medallion-architecture data lakehouse (raw, cleansed, curated layers) with data quality checks;
(c) migration of 22 existing batch jobs to the new pipeline framework;
(d) orchestration, monitoring and alerting; and
(e) documentation and a two-week knowledge transfer to Client's platform engineering team.

BlueOrchid Hotels Pvt Ltd, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office at 11th Floor, Orchid Towers, Senapati Bapat Marg, Lower Parel, Mumbai 400013, Maharashtra, India (hereinafter "BlueOrchid" or the "Client", which expression shall include its successors and permitted assigns);
AND
AtliQ Technologies Pvt Ltd, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, bearing CIN U72900MH2019PTC321456 and GSTIN 27AAKCA4821F1Z3, having its registered office at 4th Floor, Baner Business Bay, Pune 411045, Maharashtra, India (hereinafter "AtliQ" or the "Service Provider", which expression shall include its successors and permitted assigns).

AtliQ shall deliver a guest review analytics solution for all twelve (12) Properties listed in Annexure B, comprising:
(a) automated ingestion of guest reviews from up to six (6) online sources and BlueOrchid's post-stay survey tool;
(b) multilingual sentiment and aspect analysis (English, Hindi, Arabic) covering room, cleanliness, F&B, service, location and value;
(c) property-level and portfolio-level dashboards in Power BI for General Managers, the Guest Experience team and senior management;
(d) a weekly automated "Voice of Guest" summary for each Property; and
(e) an alerting mechanism flagging recurring negative themes for the relevant Property's General Manager.

Vendor shall perform the Services described in each SOW. The first SOW ("SOW-1") is attached as Exhibit B and covers:
(a) migration of Lakeshore's legacy on-premises SQL Server data warehouse to a cloud lakehouse;
(b) build of automated ingestion pipelines for point-of-sale, loyalty, inventory and e-commerce order data from all stores;
(c) a certified semantic layer for sales, margin, shrink and promotions; and
(d) Power BI dashboards for store operations, category management and executive leadership.

The Platform shall include, at a minimum, the following components:
(a) Revenue Management Module — demand forecasting at room-type and night level, dynamic rate recommendations, competitor rate ingestion, pickup and pace analysis, and a length-of-stay and overbooking optimisation engine;
(b) Guest Analytics Module — a unified guest profile consolidating data from the Company's property management system, central reservation system, loyalty programme and point-of-sale systems; guest segmentation; lifetime value scoring; and propensity models for upsell and repeat stay;
(c) Executive and Property Dashboards — Arabic and English dashboards for the Chief Commercial Officer, Revenue Managers and General Managers of each Property;
(d) Integrations — integration with the Company's existing property management system, channel manager and CRM at each Property;
(e) Training and Handover — training for up to forty (40) Company personnel across the Properties.

The Service Provider warrants that:
(a) the Services shall be performed with reasonable skill, care and diligence and in accordance with good industry practice;
(b) the Deliverables shall conform in all material respects to the specifications in Schedule 1 for a period of ninety (90) days following acceptance;
(c) it has the full right, power and authority to enter into and perform this Agreement; and
(d) it is not bound by any agreement or restriction which would prevent or restrict it from performing the Services for the Company.

WHEREAS, Covered Entity and Business Associate are parties to the Master Professional Services Agreement, Contract No. HHS-IT-2026-0193 (together with all Statements of Work and Exhibits thereto, the "Master Services Agreement"), under which Business Associate will perform services that involve the creation, receipt, maintenance or transmission of Protected Health Information on behalf of Covered Entity;
WHEREAS, Covered Entity is required by HIPAA to obtain satisfactory assurances that Business Associate will appropriately safeguard Protected Health Information;
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual promises herein and in the Master Services Agreement, the Parties agree as follows:

AtliQ shall design, develop, test and deploy the following modules into the TravelHub App production environment:
(a) Itinerary Personalization Engine — a recommendation service that generates personalised day-by-day itineraries using user preferences, trip purpose, budget, travel dates, past bookings and in-app behaviour, and re-ranks suggested activities, restaurants and experiences in real time;
(b) Partner Hotel Ranking Module — a ranking and recommendation service that scores, ranks and surfaces Partner Hotels in the United Arab Emirates and the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia to TravelHub users at the point of search and itinerary building, taking into account user fit, price competitiveness, partner commission tier, availability and conversion likelihood, and that drives the sort order of hotel results and "recommended stay" placements for booking through the TravelHub App;
(c) Partner Performance Dashboard — a dashboard for TravelHub's partnerships team showing impressions, click-through, bookings and commission by Partner Hotel, city and ranking position; and
(d) Model Operations — deployment pipelines, monitoring and a monthly retraining process for the models in (a) and (b).

WHEREAS, Client operates an integrated health system comprising acute care hospitals, ambulatory surgery centers, and outpatient clinics in the greater Houston metropolitan area;
WHEREAS, Client desires to engage Contractor to design and implement an enterprise clinical and operational analytics platform, and Contractor desires to provide such services, subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement;
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements set forth herein, and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:

Confidential Information does not include information that the Recipient can show by written records:
(a) is or becomes public through no fault of the Recipient;
(b) was known to the Recipient before disclosure without restriction;
(c) is received from a third party lawfully and without restriction; or
(d) is independently developed by the Recipient without use of the Confidential Information.

The Recipient shall:
(a) hold the Confidential Information in strict confidence and use it only for the Purpose;
(b) disclose it only to its employees who need to know it for the Purpose and who are bound by written confidentiality obligations;
(c) not copy, reverse engineer or extract the Confidential Information except as required for the Purpose;
(d) comply with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 in relation to any personal data, including health data, forming part of the Confidential Information; and
(e) notify Meridian within twenty-four (24) hours of becoming aware of any unauthorised access or disclosure.

In this Agreement:
"Brightwater Group" means Brightwater Group plc and each of its subsidiaries from time to time;
"Charges" means the charges payable for the Services as set out in Schedule 2;
"Contract Value" means the total Charges payable under this Agreement, being USD 92,000;
"Customer Data" means all data (including personal data) supplied by or on behalf of the Customer or any member of the Brightwater Group;
"Deliverables" means all outputs of the Services, including software, data models, reports and documentation;
"Good Industry Practice" means the exercise of the degree of skill, care, prudence and foresight which would reasonably be expected from a leading supplier of similar services;
"Key Dates" means the dates for delivery set out in Schedule 1;
"Services" means the services described in Schedule 1;
"Working Day" means a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or bank holiday in England or a federal holiday in the United States.

CloudSpan shall provide Partner with:
(a) twenty (20) complimentary certification vouchers per contract year;
(b) a non-production sandbox environment of the CloudSpan Platform for training and demonstration;
(c) access to the CloudSpan Partner Portal, partner-level technical support and early-access programmes; and
(d) a named partner manager.

On termination or expiry:
(a) Referral Fees for Referred Customers whose subscriptions were signed before the termination date remain payable;
(b) Clause 7 shall cease to apply from the date termination takes effect;
(c) each Party shall stop using the other's Marks; and
(d) Clauses 4.4 to 4.6, 8, 9, 12, 13, 15 and 16 survive.

Deliverables.
(a) Source-system data audit and target data model;
(b) Production pipeline (incorporating PipeKit) for WMS, telematics and TMS sources;
(c) Data-quality rules and alerting;
(d) Operational KPI dashboards (on-time dispatch, dock utilisation, fleet idle time);
(e) Runbook, technical documentation and handover training.

Each Party, as Receiving Party, shall:
(a) use the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information solely for the Purpose;
(b) not disclose it to any third party other than its Representatives who are bound by confidentiality obligations no less protective than those in this Agreement;
(c) protect it using at least the same degree of care it uses for its own confidential information, and no less than reasonable care; and
(d) promptly notify the Disclosing Party on becoming aware of any unauthorised use or disclosure.

The obligations in Clause 2 do not apply to information that the Receiving Party can demonstrate:
(a) is or becomes publicly available other than through a breach of this Agreement;
(b) was lawfully in its possession before disclosure by the Disclosing Party;
(c) is lawfully received from a third party without a duty of confidentiality; or
(d) is independently developed without use of or reference to the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information.
